     (Calibrated to empirical data: ~30-35% of disclosed CVEs remain
      unpatched at 12 months [NVD Annual Report 2023; CISA KEV data])
     Of these, 0 are CRITICAL severity.

  5. For CVEs completing full lifecycle:
     Avg pre-exploit gap   : 0.18 windows (advisory-only)
     Avg exploit window    : 1.51 windows (active danger)
     This gap is the window of opportunity for proactive patching.

  6. Reachability churn: 6 nodes became reachable due to new exploits,
     5 became unreachable due to patching.
     -> Temporal lifecycle modeling captures attack surface
        dynamics invisible to static graph analysis.

  -> No existing IDS models CVE lifecycle transitions in the
     context of temporal attack graphs. This analysis uniquely
     quantifies the window of exploitability and its structural
     impact on the TAG.
